+### Conditional grants
+
+The table keys on role and phase only, so the orchestrator names these refs in a dispatch's `inputs` when the condition holds:
+- `.asd/rules/artifact-layout.md#HTML shell wrapping (mandatory)`: a user-facing HTML artifact in the role's change surface (`asd-ba`, `asd-ux`, `asd-architect` hold it unconditionally).
+- `.asd/rules/design-system.md`, `.asd/rules/ux-principles.md`: `asd-dev` on UI input; `asd-reviewer-correctness` and `asd-reviewer-combined` for their UI section. The accessibility baseline is `inputs.ux`.
+- `asd-advisor`: only the files and sections the consulting question names (`ADVICE_NEEDED` `context`); its `checkpoints.md` grants serve gate classification alone.
+
 ### Declared tool policy
 
 An agent's declared tool policy is its own definition, plus the write allowlist a phase grants it under `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Self-hosting", plus its own memory directory (`artifact-layout.md` "Agent memory"). A dispatch payload stays inside it. An agent handed an instruction outside it returns `QUESTION` naming the contradiction — a reviewer, its question carrier per `review-policy.md` "Gate Verdict Format" — and does not comply.
